                      seon.problems-test/a-death-record-points-at-the-whole-stderr}}
 {:seon.task/name "root-boots-without-a-synthetic-program"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #50. seon.root/start! defaults :datoms 2000 (root.clj:512) and seon.db/open! seeds a fresh store with seed-tx (db.clj:17-30, 98-109): 18 namespaces app.m0..app.m17 of 20 uncontracted defns each and held app.mN/tidy tasks, written into main as program. The standing root (bin/root -> seon.check/root-serve, check.clj:1141) and every check get it, so every agent forks holding a program nobody wrote. seon.root/warm! (root.clj:484-490) queries app.m0/f1, so boot depends on the seed. Correct: start! takes no seed by default (the T5 harness already passes :datoms 0); warm! exercises a definition of its own made in a scratch namespace; a check that wants a seeded program takes a branch of the one seeded check store (seon.check/branches-as-in-production). Deletes the default and seed-tx's use outside checks."
