 {:seon.task/name "no-clip-in-renders"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #47-49. seon.render.ui/clip and line (render/ui.clj:59-65) are the clipping function the owner banned (AGENTS: no clip, subs, take n anywhere output is made for a person or a model): 24 call sites in render/ui.clj, and 4 in seon.render.ai (render/ai.clj:37,48,62-65,86: 160, 100, 140, 80 chars) inside root's own model context. Display lists drop silently: the api's view keeps :evals and :root-errors with take-last 20 (root.clj:148, 385); EVENT-CAP 60, SERIES-CAP 60, HISTORY-CAP 100 (render/proc.clj:31-35). render/ai's budget is 700 tokens times 4 chars a token (render/ai.clj:119). Correct: each clipped value gets a :seon.render/ai or :seon.render/html render on its schema, or goes through the one printer with a handle; each capped list says how many more and links to the record on main; budgets are :seon.render/budget on the view schemas, measured by the printer's own token count. Deletes clip, line and the 4-chars-a-token constant."
