 {:seon.task/name "a-stall-is-past-the-requests-own-bound"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #5-6. The stall is a guessed 30 s: seon.config STALL-MS (config.clj:54-59), checked by a go-block timer in the api's step (root.clj:449-457) and judged in the stand-in (agent_proc.clj:81-87): a 25 s compute shows nothing while a legitimate long proof run reads as stalled. The flusher waits out FLUSH-MS with Thread/sleep, pinning a fiber carrier (writer.clj:258-266). Correct: a request carries its declared bound (the form's, seon.turn/a-form-has-a-time-bound; the test run's, seon.fences/one-test-bound-derived-and-named) and the stand-in observes a stall when that bound passes with no frame: one recorded :seon.agent/stalled naming the bound, no second number. The ticks come from the one :clock proc, the flusher's included. Deletes STALL-MS."
