 {:seon.task/name "event-loss-is-counted"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #14. Root's buffers are literals in seon.root/start! (root.clj:554-560: events-in sliding 8192, :ext 1024, :back 4096, :server-ev 4096, :judge 64), seon.root/events taps sliding 1024 and are never untapped (root.clj:647), render's tap is sliding 4096 (render/proc.clj:512). A sliding buffer drops the oldest with no count, so the dashboard can miss events and nothing says so. Correct (the step-fn law: buffers bounded by their loss semantics): every buffer is declared in resources/seon/system.edn :chan-opts with its loss; a sliding buffer counts its drops into the api's view (:events-dropped by tap) shown on the dashboard; c/events taps are released with their reader. Estimate: one counter per drop."
