 {:seon.task/name "fork-refusal-names-the-threads"
  :seon.task/plan "Audit FENCES #15-16. seon.lib/safe-fork 1000 (lib.clj:257-262; used at agent.clj:311, 446) spins 50 us x 20,000 hoping a second Chez thread ends, then answers -2 and the agent says another thread stayed busy for 1 s (a running future?). An agent is single-threaded by physics (DRAGONS: who may run threads), so a second thread is a defect to name, not to wait out. seon.agent interrupt-self-test (agent.clj:251) spins up to 100,000 (eval 1) waiting for its own SIGUSR1. Correct: safe-fork checks lib/active-threads once and answers a typed :seon.agent/not-single-threaded {:active-threads n} at once (the test run and clone report it); the self-test waits on one safe point (one engine tick) and records whether the handler ran. Deletes the 1000 ms and the 100,000."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.agent-test/a-fork-beside-a-thread-is-refused-at-once-naming-it
                      seon.agent-test/the-interrupt-self-test-needs-one-safe-point}}]
